---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
---
<Base title="Accessibility" description="How theluxuryliners.com is built to be accessible, and how to tell us about a problem.">
  <PageHead title="Accessibility" size="l">
    <p class="lede">We want everyone to be able to use this site. It aims to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA.</p>
  </PageHead>
  <div class="wrap page-body">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h3">What we do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Every page works without JavaScript, with the keyboard alone and on small screens.</li>
        <li>Every photo has a text description; every cover is named.</li>
        <li>Links are underlined, and the keyboard focus is always visible.</li>
        <li>There is a light and a dark theme. The site follows your device’s setting, and the “Dark theme” switch at the top of each page (it needs JavaScript) changes it.</li>
        <li>Animations are switched off when your device asks for reduced motion.</li>
        <li>Videos load only when you press play.</li>
        <li>Every page is checked with the axe accessibility engine, in both themes, each time the site is built, and a page that fails is not published.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 class="h3">Tell us about a problem</h2>
      <p>If something on the site doesn’t work for you, please use the <a href="/contact/?topic=accessibility">contact form</a> and choose “Accessibility problem”. Tell us the page and what happened.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
